the sheep assumes the  position on his behalf now the ambiance  turns towards the predators in town and  the animals have to deal with fear  however julian nick find out that  bellwether is to blame for everything as  she holds a grudge against the  carnivores and does intend to get rid of  them together they manage to foil her  plan and nick ends up joining the zpd  himself  unfortunately we don't know anything  about the exact plot yet but there are  some rumors floating around about the  second part of zootopia and also the  online community has some ideas besides  it can be said that the social topics  addressed and the first part alone can  be further expanded in an interview with  cinema blend nick's voice actor jason  bateman already revealed that the two of  them will tidy up the streets as  partners there are some new cops out  there he added so bad guys be warned  thus it is evident who will be in the  thick of the action once again judy and  mick  but not only as official partners at the  zpd as there seems to be something else  going on between the two of them after  all the first part ends with nick  claiming that judy knows she has a crush  on him which she confirms so pretty much  everyone agrees that there will be some  kind of love story developing around the  two of them who knows this might even be  something special in zootopia so far we  know that only animals of the same breed  have ever become a couple and here we  are actually talking about two hostile  species nowadays this would of course  strike a chord again if the movie  addressed topics such as free love and  different sexualities in general they  could take up the topic of gender one  more time and explore in more depth judy  is the only bunny working for the police  and besides officer francine the  elephant she's also the only female who  seems to be working for the authorities  in general most of the animals we  encounter are male besides her and  francine we only see the star singer  gazelle the concerned mrs otterton and  mafia heiress frufu and don bellwether  this could be a neat transition to  sexism in society  we also hope that the two partners will  finally make it to the areas of zootopia  that haven't been shown yet although  we're told at the beginning of the film  that zootopia is a huge city we only get  to see downtown rainforest district and  tundratown in the course of the first  movie yet there are many more urban  areas to explore like the camel district  canyonland marshlands meadowlands polo  strait and sahara square however the  capital city is not the one that should  be of interest for the upcoming  storyline we actually do not know  anything yet about the planet or the  continent in which the movie takes place  sure there were a couple of scenes in  bunny burb but that's it there's still  an entire world to discover besides so  far only mammals have been featured in  part one what about other species like  fish reptiles and insects in case these  creatures really exist the second film  could deal with the question of why they  were excluded from zootopia and  re-examine the topic of xenophobia  a somewhat sensitive topic could be that  of class society at first glance  everything in zootopia seems to look  like love peace and harmony yet just by  looking at nick and his accomplice at  the beginning of the film it seems that  there are animals who have to earn their  money in a shady way in the city of  endless opportunities and so there's for  instance also a mafia in zootopia a  story about this would be particularly  suitable for nick in his old life after  all until he met judy he was not really  doing any honest work you say the gap  between rich and poor might be too  severe for an animated film well then  don't forget one of the core messages of  the first film in an amusing way it  shows how racism is a fear that is  promoted by those in power therefore the  next part could well try its luck with  other serious topics  what most of you probably do not know is  that zootopia was originally intended to  be a spy movie where a spy arrives on a  mysterious island in a world full of  mammals perhaps it could be a storyline  for the sequel and why not it's not cast  in stone that nick and judy have to stay  with the zpd forever especially nick  could be well pictured in the role of  his secret agent the second part could  easily revert from buddy cop comedy to  the originally envisioned spy genre  so now we've heard a few possibilities  of how the plot could go on but what  does the fan community on reddit  actually say there one theory has  prevailed namely that we will meet  nick's father in the course of the film  and that the latter will be arrested by  judy when the interrogation reveals who  it is nick falls back into his old  behavior patterns the rest of the movie  will then delve into nick and his  father's past and find answers as to why  he abandoned him before he was even born  in general fans on reddit are crying out  to know more about this live fox  but when is zootopia 2 coming opinions  differ on this because disney has not  even officially confirmed the second  part some years ago they probably would  not have even thought of making a sequel  but since wreck-it ralph and frozen they  are considering a theatrical sequel  looking at the numbers this would only  be natural as zootopia was one of the  most successful movies from the disney  animation studios in the last 10 years  here it is worth noting that december  21st 2022 is a day that will see the  release of a disney animated film about  which nothing else has been announced  yet anyways it is safe to say that  zootopia 2 will not be hitting theaters  before the end of 2022 as soon as we  know more you will of course be notified  in our weekly news  well here we go those were all the  theories about the second part of  zootopia which idea do you think is the  best so far and do you have any other  suggestions on how it could continue let  us know in the comments if you enjoyed  this video feel free to give us a thumbs  up and if you don't want to miss any  more of our videos you might want to  subscribe to us see you next time bye  [Music]  you

